title ALES189 — Lotus's stereo_reverb_ms: ALES187's linked stereo Schroeder network spoken in MILLISECONDS, a thin twin fusing reverb_ms's two-bank conversion with stereo_echo_time's stereo delegation
prompt Continue the recursion loop on the ALES / Lotus edge, Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round; stop at custody gates.
think ALES188 (reverb_ms) landed the mono timed reverb this same loop; stereo_reverb.rye's own header named the stereo timed twin as the road ahead ("a real-time stereo twin through the ALES5 clock is a later rung, exactly as stereo_echo_time followed stereo_echo"). Lindy-first crux-first: this thin twin completes the timed reverb family, so the reverb speaks the keeper's own units on both channels.
think stereo_reverb_ms fuses two proven patterns: the two-bank conversion of ALES188's reverb_ms (check bank counts first, convert each comb/allpass delay_ms through clock.samples_for into an index-named bank) and the stereo delegation of ALES182's stereo_echo_ms (one shared conversion feeds both channels, then delegate to the proven stereo tool). It REUSES ALES188's CombSpecMs/AllpassSpecMs as the timed spec types — one source of truth for the millisecond-named reverb stage, no redefinition.
think StereoReverbTimeError = clock.ClockError || reverb.ReverbError, no new fault. The balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit; the shared conversion holds the image for free. delegated to stereo_reverb which validates the whole bank once against the shared length before either channel is touched, so a refusal never reverbs one channel and tears the other.
think Proved six laws: the clock adds only units (both channels == ALES187's index-named stereo reverb byte for byte, both tools run, channels genuinely differing); a real 48 kHz rate converts 1 ms to 48 samples on both, the first recirculation exactly there (left 10000->5000, right 6000->3000); the identical-channel image law (a centred master staying identical, the panned ratio honestly NOT claimed — inherited from ALES187's @divTrunc recirculation note); a sub-sample comb refuses BadDelay; an allpass delay past the clip refuses DurationTooLong with a valid comb ahead of it; the reverb's bank faults forward (NoCombs, BadGain, BadRange), each leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count_ms 0 the identity.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal pass, TAME bans clean, width exit 0, ALES187 stereo reverb re-run GREEN beside it. The timed reverb family now stands whole in mono and stereo. Purely local, siloed to lotus/; no cross-channel read, socket, network, keys, funds, device, or hardware clock claim — no custody gate reached, a self-approved design round.
